        			</tr>
        		</table>
        		<script language="javascript" type="text/javascript">
        	function checkChildren(srcObj, vType) {
        		for (var i = 0; i < eval("document.formSMC." + vType + ".length"); i++) {
        			if ((eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].value.substring(0, srcObj.length)") == srcObj) && (eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].disabled") == false)) {
        					(eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].checked")) ? eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = false : eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = true;
        			}
        		}
        		return false;
        	}
        function toggleRepealed(element) {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        		else {
        			row.classList.remove('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        function HideRepealed() {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        </script>
        <div style="padding: 15px;"><form action="/smc/" method="post" name="formSMC">
        <div id="hideRepealed">
        		<p><a href="/smc/?Title=17G">Title 17G</a> Administration and Procedures</p>
        				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=17G.010">Chapter 17G.010</a> Building and Construction Permits</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.010">Section 17G.010.010</a> Exemption from Permits<br />
        <p>Exemption from a permit requirement is not exemption from the other requirements of this code.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 21, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 30, 2005</p><p>ORD C33578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.020">Section 17G.010.020</a> Validity of Permits<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>The issuance of a permit or acceptance of plans, specifications and computations shall not be construed to be a permit for, or an approval of, any violation of any of the provisions of this code or of other ordinances of the City. No permit presuming to give authority to violate or cancel the provisions of this code is valid.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The issuance of a permit based upon plans, specifications, computations and other data does not prevent the director from thereafter requiring the correction of errors in said plans, specifications and other data, or from preventing construction or building operations being carried on thereunder when in violation of this code or of other ordinances of the City. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 21, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 30, 2005</p><p>ORD C33578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.030">Section 17G.010.030</a> Expiration of Building Permits<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Every permit issued by the Development Services Department under the provisions of this code will expire by limitation and become null and void if the work authorized by such permit is not commenced within one hundred eighty days from the date of such permit. Evidence of commencement would be an inspection entry on an issued permit or verification via a physical site visit by the Building Official or their representative.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Issued permits in which work has commenced within one hundred eighty days of issuance are valid for two calendar years from issuance date.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Courtesy Notices are sent in the mail to permit holders at least thirty days or more prior to the first expiration date<u>,</u> telling the permit holder to call for inspections or request for extensions if additional time is needed. If the permit holder fails to obtain the necessary inspections or request extensions by the permit expiration date, the work will be presumed to be abandoned<u>,</u> and the permit will expire by default.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A permittee holding an unexpired permit may apply for an extension of the time within which they may commence work under that permit when he is unable to commence work within the time required by this section for good and satisfactory reasons. The Building Official may extend the time for action by the permittee for a period not exceeding one hundred eighty days upon written or verbal request by the permittee identifying the circumstances necessary for the extension request.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">In order to renew action on a permit after expiration, the permittee must pay a new permit fee. Guidelines in&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.02.031" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">SMC 8.02.031(U)</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&nbsp;will be followed.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, November 28, 2025</p><p>ORD C36753 Section 41</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.040">Section 17G.010.040</a> Expiration of Building Permit Plan Review<br />
        <p>An application for a permit for any proposed work shall be deemed to have been abandoned one hundred eighty days after the date of filing, unless such application has been pursued in good faith or a permit has been issued; except that the building official is authorized to grant one or more extensions of time for additional periods not exceeding ninety days each. The extension shall be requested in writing and justifiable cause demonstrated. (Reference 2012 IBC 105.3.2)</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 24, 2013</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, July 1, 2013</p><p>ORD C34996 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.050">Section 17G.010.050</a> Suspension or Revocation of Permits<br />
        <p>The director may in writing suspend or revoke a permit issued under the provisions of this title whenever the permit is issued in error or on the basis of incorrect information supplied or in violation of other ordinance or regulation of the City.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 21, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 30, 2005</p><p>ORD C33578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.060">Section 17G.010.060</a> Applicability to Single and Multifamily Residential Buildings<br />
        <p>All local amendments to the codes adopted herein which apply to new construction of single and multifamily residential buildings shall not be effective until approved by the State Building Code Council. The local amendment is:</p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.040.120">SMC 17F.040.120</a> on roof design. </li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 21, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 30, 2005</p><p>ORD C33578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.070">Section 17G.010.070</a> Eligibility of Applicants – Permits Issued Pursuant to the Land Use Codes<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The laws of various jurisdictions impose requirements upon the persons doing some of the work and conducting some of the activities regulated by this title. Many of the acts regulated by this title affect real property interests. For these reasons applicants for the various permits, licenses, certificates, and other approvals are required to furnish varying data concerning their authority to make the application and perform the acts applied for. The City does not, however, assume responsibility for the accuracy of an applicant&rsquo;s representations concerning entitlement to the approval applied for. The issuance of a permit, license, certificate, or other approval to a person not otherwise authorized does not operate to confer such authority.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Building Permits</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">To be eligible to obtain any of the various categories of &ldquo;building&rdquo; permits, one must be:</span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A contractor with a City of Spokane business license and an active contractor&rsquo;s license from the State of Washington Department of Labor and Industries that is appropriate for the work to be performed; or</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The property owner as identified by the Spokane County Assessor records on condition that;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the owner is able to claim exemption from the State of Washington contractor registration requirements; and</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">all work is being performed by the owner and others as allowed by law, or by persons duly licensed or certified where required for the nature of the work.</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Exception: Mechanical and boiler permits for any work involving gas piping, equipment, or appliances that are natural gas, liquid propane gas, or oil fueled can only be issued to appropriately licensed contractors unless the property owner is currently licensed by the City of Spokane to install such piping, equipment, or appliances.</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Encroachments in Public Ways.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Applications for building projections, sidewalk openings, fences, or other encroachments under <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.140" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 17G.010.140</a> must be made by or on behalf of all property owners as described in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.070" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 17G.010.070</a>.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Certificates of Occupancy</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Applications for certificates of occupancy may be made by any owner, contractor, lessee, tenant, mortgagee, trust deed beneficiary, or representative having the right of possession or right-of-entry.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Safety Certifications</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Applications for safety or code compliance certifications may be made by any owner, contractor, lessee, tenant, mortgagee, trust deed beneficiary, or representative having the right of possession or right-of-entry.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Contractor Licenses.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The eligibility of licensees as contractors is set forth in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.190" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 17G.010.190</a>.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Workers Licenses.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The eligibility of licensees as regulated workers is set forth in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.200" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 17G.010.200</a>.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="8" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Special Construction Activities.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The eligibility of permittees for special construction activities is set forth in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.210" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 17G.010.210</a>.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Wednesday, February 24, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, January 11, 2016</p><p>ORD C35342 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.080">Section 17G.010.080</a> Stop Work Order<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>The director may order suspended any work which is not being performed in strict compliance with the approval or applicable law and may require the applicant, his agent or surety, to take such action, including without limitation vacating the premises, erection of barricades and posting of guards, as may be warranted to avoid or eliminate undue hazard.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Such an order is served on such persons and in such manner as is reasonable under the circumstances, it is at least posted at the site. As soon as practical such order is made in writing. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 21, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 30, 2005</p><p>ORD C33578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.090">Section 17G.010.090</a> Cost of Enforcement<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">In addition to the various permit, license, inspection and other application fees which are designed and intended to at least partially defray the cost of administration and which, therefore, are not refundable, except as provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.02.0692">SMC 8.02.0692</a>, the City declares its right and intention to claim reimbursement for extraordinary expenses incurred as a result of a person&rsquo;s acts or omissions in violation of this code. The City may claim costs incurred in judicial proceedings and may claim against any public liability, indemnity, or performance insurance policy or bond.<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">Whenever the City is reasonably required to cure defective work or a hazardous condition in or about a public way, the City may charge its costs and expenses against any owner of the abutting property or a contractor or other agent doing the work or creating the condition. To the extent that such work done by the City relieves the abutting property owner of potential liability, the City claims the right to file liens against such property pursuant to any laws conferring the right of lien on persons whose furnishing of labor or materials benefits the property of another.<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">Notwithstanding any other ordinances or statutes providing for real property liens, the City&rsquo;s cost of repairs, alterations, improvements, removal, demolition, vacating or closing unfit or unsafe buildings shall be assessed against the real property upon which the cost was incurred, and, when filed with the Spokane county treasurer become a part of the general taxes for that year, to be collected at the same time and with interest as provided by statute.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 21, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 30, 2005</p><p>ORD C33578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.100">Section 17G.010.100</a> Types of Permits<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Construction and Development.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person needs a building permit (which may be in the form of a factory-built or manufactured housing permit as well as a standard building permit) and also, depending upon the circumstances of the particular case, some combination of demolition, grading, sign, swimming pool, parking lot, and site preparation, building moving and relocation, street encroachment, boiler installation and operating, electrical, elevator installation and operating, storage tank installation, private fire hydrant installation, mechanical, plumbing, side sewer installation and connection, water line tapping, shoreline development permits, flood management permits, street address assignment, and a variety of similar approvals for new construction or placement, alteration, repair or demolition of a building, structure or other improvement to land; and for the new installation, alteration, repair or operation of a building&rsquo;s boiler, electrical, elevator, fire protection, mechanical and plumbing systems.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Private fire hydrants are approved by the Water and Hydroelectric Services Department based on compliance with design standards and regulations established by the fire official and the Director of Engineering Services.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Side sewers and connections are approved by the Engineering Services Department based on compliance with the sewer code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Storage tank permits are issued by the fire official based on compliance with the fire code and various environmental and aquifer protection measures.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Water line taps are approved by the Engineering Services Department based on review by the Water and Hydroelectric Services Department and compliance with the water code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="5" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Street addresses are assigned by the Engineering Services Department.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="6" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Type II permits<u>,</u> as specified in&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=17G.061" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">chapter 17G.061&nbsp;SMC</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&nbsp;are issued by the Director of Planning Services and Type III permits as specified in&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=17G.061" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">chapter 17G.061&nbsp;SMC</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&nbsp;are granted by the Hearing Examiner. Shorelines permits are subject to approval by the Washington State Department of Ecology.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="7" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Commercial driveway permits are issued by the Director of Engineering Services.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="8" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The other building and development permits are issued by the Development Services Department, Planning and Economic Development Services Department, and Engineering Services Department based on compliance of the application, plans, specifications, diagrams and drawings with the requirements of the applicable provisions of this title and any rules and regulations promulgated thereunder.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Flood management permits are issued by the Director of Planning Services and subject to approval by the Washington State Department of Ecology and the Federal Emergency Management Act&rsquo;s National Flood Insurance Program.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="10" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A separate demolition permit shall be issued with each building permit that involves any demolition activities.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person needs an approved plat, binding site plan, or short plat to divide or segregate a parcel of land into two or more lots or parcels for such purposes as sale or lease, unless the activity is specifically exempted under&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.080.020" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">SMC 17G.080.020(B)</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">. A person needs an approved conditional use permit or planned unit development to group or cluster buildings on a lot or combination of lots.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Conditional use permits, plans-in-lieu of compliance, and certificates of compliance are approved by the Hearing Examiner or the Director of Planning Services, and planned unit developments are approved by the Hearing Examiner on the basis of compliance of the plans with the applicable provisions of this title and pertinent rules and regulations.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Plats are approved by the Hearing Examiner; short plats, binding site plans, and boundary line adjustments are approved by the Director of Planning Services on the basis of compliance with the applicable provisions of this title and administrative rules and regulations.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Preliminary planned unit developments are approved by the Hearing Examiner.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Variances are approved by the Hearing Examiner.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person needs approval to construct, install, alter, or relocate any building or structure, or some part or equipment thereof, within, beneath, or over the right-of-way of a public way. Approval is given by the Development Services Department in accordance with the building code, flood insurance regulations, utilities code, and various other laws relating to streets and highways, utilities, traffic, and public safety. When design review is required pursuant to&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=17G.040" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">chapter 17G.040 SMC</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">, the approval of the Director of Planning Services is also required.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person may need additional approvals determined by the use classification, occupancy group, construction type, size, location, or other feature of a building, structure<u>,</u> or activity, including structures located in the one-hundred-year floodplain. Such special approvals issue from numerous federal, state, regional, or local public agencies based on a variety of laws.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Use and Occupancy of Property.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person needs a certificate of occupancy to establish or change, or allow to be established or changed, any occupancy of land or any building or portion thereof. A certificate of occupancy is issued by the Development Services Department with approval of the Spokane Fire Department and Planning and Economic Development Services Department when the occupancy complies with the building code, fire code<u>,</u> and the land use codes.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person needs a variance or a certificate of compliance from the Director of Planning Services or Hearing Examiner to render lawful proposed or existing structures which do not comply with the locational or dimensional standards of the zoning code, shoreline master program or flood hazard ordinance.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person needs the proper zoning classification (or design plan designation) and<u>,</u> in some cases<u>,</u> a conditional use permit or planned unit development approval to establish or maintain, or allow to be established or maintained, any use of land and buildings.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Zone classifications are established by the City Council upon recommendation of the Plan Commission or Hearing Examiner.<u> </u></span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Conditional use permits are granted by the Director of Planning Services or the Hearing Examiner.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Preliminary planned unit developments are approved by the Hearing Examiner. Final planned unit developments are subject to approval by ordinance of the &nbsp;City Council. Plans-in-lieu of compliance are approved by the Director of Planning Services or Hearing Examiner in accordance with the comprehensive plan, zoning code<u>,</u> and environmental policy code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person may need special approvals, which may include bonds or other security devices, and may be required to meet various conditions and standards, to establish, change, or maintain certain uses, occupations, or activities upon property, depending upon the definition of the activity, as provided by numerous federal, state, regional and local regulatory programs.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person is required to maintain buildings, land, and premises in satisfaction of minimum standards prescribed by the existing buildings and conservation code, the fire code, conditions imposed under the land use codes, and various other laws relating to public health and safety and nuisance.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Construction Activities and Contractors.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">General and specialty contractors are required to be registered with the state under chapter 18.27 RCW, and such registration is a prerequisite for the issuance of any building permit. Some contractors are also subject to special regulations by the state. A person needs a license from the City to operate as a contractor using explosives. The blaster&rsquo;s license is issued by the Director of Engineering Services and may be revoked by the Director of Engineering Services or by the fire official under the license code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person needs a permit, license, or certificate to practice the trade or be engaged in the occupation of:</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Installing or servicing heating, cooling, and ventilating systems;</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Operating steam boilers; or</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Operating aircraft refueler units.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Such licenses are issued by the Development Services Department in accordance with the standards set forth in the license code or by the fire official as provided in the fire code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A person needs a permit, license, or certificate to practice the trade or be engaged in the occupation of:</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha; margin-left:40px">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Installing, or servicing, or using gas or oil fuels;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha; margin-left:40px">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Maintaining or altering fire equipment systems;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha; margin-left:40px">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Testing underground storage tanks.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha; margin-left:40px">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Such licenses are issued by the Spokane Fire Department in accordance with the standards set forth in the license code or by the fire official as provided in the fire code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">In addition to a building permit or land use permit, a person needs a specific permit for:</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Blasting,</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Moving a building,</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Installing or connecting a sewer,</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Installing or altering fire protection or detection equipment, and</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="5" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Obstructing a street.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, November 28, 2025</p><p>ORD C36753 Section 42</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.110">Section 17G.010.110</a> Ministerial Permit Categorically Exempt from the State Environmental Policy Act (SEPA)<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">This group of ministerial permits and certificates includes those issued by the building official, the engineering services director, planning and economic development services director, historic preservation officer, fire marshal, street director and other administrative officials for construction and development. However, this category of permits relates only to development projects so minor in scope as to be categorically exempt from the requirement of the Washington State Environmental Policy Act for a threshold determination. Permit applications of this type are reviewed for compliance with specifically prescribed construction standards, as well as other provisions of the Spokane Municipal Code. An applicant is entitled to any such permit that conforms to those prescribed standards and provisions.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 21, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 30, 2005</p><p>ORD C33578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.120">Section 17G.010.120</a> Ministerial Permits Not Categorically Exempt from SEPA and Discretionary Permits<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">This group of ministerial and discretionary permits includes those issued by the building official, the engineering services director and the director of planning. This category of permits related to development that is subject to the one hundred twenty day time limits required by chapter 36.70B RCW and including ministerial permits subject to SEPA and discretionary permits, regardless of whether SEPA is required. The permit application, review, decision and notice provisions for these applications are provided in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=17G.061">chapter 17G.061&nbsp;SMC</a>.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 21, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 30, 2005</p><p>ORD C33578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.130">Section 17G.010.130</a> Application Submission Requirements – Ministerial Permits Exempt from SEPA<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">Each permit application subject to this chapter includes a general application providing the information specified by the permitting department. Each application also includes one or more supplemental applications for the specific permit(s) requested and provides the information described in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.140">SMC 17G.010.140</a> through <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.230">17G.010.230</a>. A permit application is not considered complete and is not reviewed or heard until such information and material as required by these sections is submitted and all required fees are paid. If an application is determined to be incomplete, the applicant is notified in writing within seven days. The notice identifies the missing material or information necessary to complete the application.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 21, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 30, 2005</p><p>ORD C33578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.140">Section 17G.010.140</a> Applicant Requirements<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Applications for ministerial permits categorically exempt from the threshold determination requirements of the State Environmental Policy Act (SEPA) are submitted to the permit authority<u>,</u> reviewed according to the provisions of this title or Spokane Municipal Code chapters. Depending upon the nature of the application, the permit authority might be the Building Official, fire official, Director of Streets, Director of Planning Services, or Engineering Services Director.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">An applicant for building (and/or boiler, electrical, elevator, grading, mechanical, plumbing, sign) permit shall pay the prescribed fees and file an application upon forms furnished by the Development Services Department, which application:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">identifies and describes the work to be covered by the permit;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">describes the property on which the proposed work is to be done by legal description and street address assigned by the Engineering Services Department or similar description that will readily identify and definitely locate the proposed building or work;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">indicates the use or occupancy for which the proposed work is intended;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">is accompanied by plans, diagrams, computations, specifications, and other data as required;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">states the valuation of any new building or structure or any addition, remodeling, or alteration to an existing building; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">identifies by name the owner and occupant of the premises.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The applicant shall submit with each application, plans, engineering calculations, diagrams, specifications, and other data as necessary, drawn to scale, where applicable, upon substantial paper or cloth by a registered architect or professional engineer of sufficient clarity to indicate the location, nature and extent of the work proposed, and showing in detail that the work will conform to the provisions of all applicable laws. The data to be submitted under this subsection include, in the case of:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">an electrical permit, the nature and kind of electric wiring, apparatus, fixtures, and equipment to be installed, altered<u>,</u> or extended;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">installation of a boiler or unfired pressure vessel, manufacturer&rsquo;s data reports;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">a permit for a sign, the location of the property line and building line, curb distance<u>,</u> and height above grade;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">a building permit, a plot plan to scale showing the actual dimensions of the lot and the size, use<u>,</u> and location of existing and proposed buildings;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">street obstruction or construction permission where design review is required pursuant to&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=17G.040" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">chapter 17G.040 SMC</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">, a written statement from the Director of Planning Services&nbsp;indicating compliance with the design review process.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The Building Official may waive or modify the requirements for an application as the nature of the work applied for dictates.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, November 28, 2025</p><p>ORD C36753 Section 43</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17G.010.150">Section 17G.010.150</a> Special Application Requirements for Commercial Building Permits<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="display:none">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">General.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">An owner, or the owner&rsquo;s architect, engineer<u>,</u> or other agent, should consult with the Development Services Department, Engineering Services Department, and Planning and Economic Development Services Department before submitting an application for a commercial building permit to identify any peculiar considerations and discussing any special requirements. The owner, or the owner&rsquo;s architect, engineer<u>,</u> or other agent<u>,</u> must submit ten prints of the site plan, and three each of the architectural plan, structural plan, and mechanical plan stamped by an architect or engineer licensed in the State of Washington, to the Development Services Department. The Development Services Department transmits copies of the print to other departments and agencies as appropriate. The following information is required for a complete application for a commercial building permit. The information needs to be provided on the site plan or front sheet of plans in the numbered order given. The Building Official may waive or modify specific submittal requirements determined to be unnecessary for review of an application.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Name of project and date of application.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Official street address. If an official street address has not been assigned, it must be obtained from the Engineering Services Department.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Name, address<u>,</u> and phone number of the architect.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Name, address<u>,</u> and phone number of the owner and agent.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Name, address<u>,</u> and phone number of the tenant.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Name, address<u>,</u> and phone number of the engineer(s).</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="7">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Name, address<u>,</u> and phone number of the consultant(s).</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="8">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Name, address<u>,</u> and phone number of the contractor(s).</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="9">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Name, address<u>,</u> and phone number of the contact person.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="10">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Project type, new, remodel, addition<u>,</u> or alteration.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="11">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Existing use of lot and/or building.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="12">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Proposed use(s).</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="13">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Number of dwelling units.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="14">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Occupancy group and division.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="15">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Construction type required.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="16">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Building allowable height and area.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="17">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Building height (both in feet and number of stories).</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="18">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Basement floor area and occupant load.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="19">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Ground floor area and occupant load.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="20">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Floor area of each story above ground floor and occupant load (list each story individually).</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="21">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Total floor area, including basements and occupied roofs.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="22">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Valuation.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="23">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">SEPA checklist, if required.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="24">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Critical materials, if involved.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="25">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">HMMP plan submitted, if required.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="26">
